From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:33:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: Add MediaTek MT6358 fuel gauge driver

Add a driver for the coulomb counter fuel gauge of the MediaTek MT6358
and MT6366 PMICs.

The gauge reports the battery current, and integrates it in a 32-bit
two's complement counter with 11 fractional bits; one count is
108507 / 2048 nAh with the reference 10 mOhm shunt. Both are read under
the gauge's latch so that they belong to the same instant.

The state of charge is seeded from the battery's OCV table: the loaded
voltage, averaged over a few samples, is corrected by the internal
resistance and the current into an open circuit voltage. From then on
the charge follows the coulomb counter, and is set to full whenever the
charger supplying the battery reports that charging has finished. That
check comes first, so a phone that boots on a charger in constant
voltage regulation, where the loaded voltage lies above the whole OCV
table, starts at full rather than from a voltage estimate; otherwise an
OCV beyond either end of the table reads as 100% or 0%. The
driver never resets the counter: it works with differences from the
count at the last anchor, so it does not depend on the state the
bootloader left the counter in.

Prior art: Roman Vivchar's MT6358 gauge driver in the mt6768-mainline
tree, and MediaTek's vendor mt6358-gauge driver for the register layout
and units.

Signed-off-by: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
